**S16. Real 013/014 overlap check tool, ready to run** (model: Sol)
- Goal: a one-command runner (Linux sh + Windows pwsh -NoProfile -File) that our NNUE bot can run on the PC. It runs the Job D filter over D's output plus every sealed shard against 013/014, counts overlap by position hash and by game group, and writes a removal list. Add the fixes from QA_sol_jobD_return_20261025.md:
  - fail closed on interleaved text;
  - a --work-dir for the SQLite scratch DB;
  - a free-disk precheck (about 300 B/row);
  - a conflicting-label duplicate counter;
  - a whole-shard md5 duplicate check.
- Inputs: files/09_sol_returns/sol_return_jobACD_20261025/ (filter + tests), files/09_sol_returns/QA_sol_jobD_return_20261025.md, files/06_jobD/ (format, holdout note, samples, 916-line text), files/07_nnue_context/train_resid_v3b.py.
- Deliver: forge_sol_S16_overlap_runner_<date>.{sh,ps1}, a NEW filter version forge_sol_datafilter_v2_<date>.py + tests, report.
- Pass: the 21 old tests plus the new ones pass; it reproduces 157,666 kept of 200k at t300 on the sample; output md5s are deterministic; the real counts are marked UNVERIFIED.

**S26. Net-pack batch script** (model: Sol; was Astra A5, moved by crew vote 8/8 at 10:30)
- Goal: one script that, for a list of .inc nets, reports:
  - net md5/sha256;
  - bench at the 5 depths;
  - FMA count;
  - WAC 1000 ms score;
  - ctest with a known-fail allowlist FILE (WAC001 ×2, rook underpromotion ×2; pins format ready for S1's later pin change).
  It writes one table per net.
- Inputs: files/03b_nets_f019_f023_s197_s198/, files/03_nets/, files/10_cr/CR_BATCH_nnue_f020-f023.txt, CR_PASS_nnue_e20f019.txt, CR_PASS_nnue_e32f003rec_s197.txt, CR_PASS_nnue_e32f003rec_s198.txt, files/10_cr/cr_bench.sh, files/13_coder/packer_snap_a07f1972/, files/12_strength/h256tools/ (WAC300).
- Deliver: forge_sol_S26_netbatch_<date>.sh (+ .py helpers), allowlist file, sample output for f019-f023, report.
- Pass:
  - reproduces the CR f019-f023 numbers (bench exact, WAC within 3);
  - writes only inside its own out dir;
  - runs at nice 19, 1 core, under a flock lock file;
  - stops cleanly below 3 GB free RAM;
  - no host-limit changes.

**S27. Patch hygiene pre-check** (model: Sol; was Astra A6, moved by crew vote 8/8 at 10:30)
- Goal: a script that takes a patch (or zip) and checks that it:
  - applies with -p1 -F0 to L and B;
  - contains no LICENSE/copyright text and no "OpenAI";
  - writes nothing under baseline/, dist-v* or lock dirs;
  - adds no new code to the default build outside #if/option guards (heuristic + a build-and-compare mode: default-build exe symbols/uci list/bench output vs base);
  - has every new option in the uci list;
  - does not have the same hash as an earlier reviewed patch (hash list file);
  - has no prefix…suffix hashes in its docs.
- Inputs: files/10_cr/sol_patchset_b425207a/, files/10_cr/cr_sol_int16_dc5ff59/, files/10_cr/cr_sol_jobCA_a0b6811f/, files/02_buffix/fc_sol_buffix_h256e12_vs_lock.patch, the Job A and Job C patches in files/09_sol_returns/.
- Deliver: forge_sol_S27_hygiene_<date>.py + known-hash list + tests + report.
- Pass:
  - flags Job A's default-build counters/option/stats line;
  - flags a Sol-style source zip that adds an MIT LICENSE naming the vendor. The original zip (sha256 prefix f7a145738b36cf4e, described in files/10_cr/sol_patchset_b425207a/CR_HOLD_sol_nnueint16_b425207a.txt) is NOT in this zip, so build that fixture at test time; don't ship the literal text;
  - PASSES the buffer-only (buffix) patch and the Job C patch;
  - zero false positives on those two;
  - deterministic.

astra_jobs.spec_verbatim:
**A1. Correction-history / history rework** (tally 22; DR J5 + Strategist J6 + Strength S4)
- Goal: ONE new OFF-default option (default 0 = lock behaviour) that reworks how the correction and history tables learn and blend. Possible parts:
  - gravity-style update retune;
  - continuation correction (previous move piece+to);
  - a correction blend keyed on pawn structure and on non-pawn material/structure;
  - threat-keyed quiet history.
  Include 2-3 tune steps (option values) and a written PROOF of no integer overflow: worst-case bounds for every table and every product/sum in update and read, with the int widths used.
- Our previous attempts were all close to 0 or parked. Read why first and don't resubmit them:
  - contcorr ("barely minus" -1.4; patch + CR in files/15_prior_corrhist/);
  - NonPawnCorr / PawnHist / LmrCorrThreshold (QUEUE_PENDING rework list);
  - CorrGravity (QUEUE_PENDING line about update_correction).
- Current code: L src/search.cpp, corrected_eval and update_correction near lines 638-656 and 1218-1222; tune:: params near lines 25-100.
- Inputs: L, B, files/15_prior_corrhist/, files/08_status/QUEUE_PENDING.md, files/11_ideas_profile/FORGE_IDEA_BOARD.md, files/10_cr/CR_PASS_contcorr_h256e12.txt.
- Deliver:
  - forge_astra_A1_corrhist_<date>.patch;
  - forge_astra_A1_design_<date>.md (idea, IDEA_SOURCE, overflow proof, tuning ranges, why it differs from contcorr/NonPawnCorr);
  - forge_astra_A1_sprt_plan_<date>.md (which values to gate first, at 10+0.1 [0,10] cap 1500, and a longer-TC confirm);
  - report.
- Pass: Std pass; every ON value changes nodes (state the d11/d13 nodes); ON 5-depth sweep has no blowup (> 1.5x nodes vs OFF at d20/22 = flag); UBSan clean with ON values at their max; a unit test hits the overflow bounds.

**A3. Full-NNUE design + trainer + converter + smoke net, NO engine integration yet** (tally 24; Strategist J1; reworked by crew vote 6/8 at 10:30). Start only after YOUR A2 design doc is finished.
- Goal: everything a later full NNUE (king-bucketed inputs per A2, float accumulator, 1-2 hidden layers, 8 output buckets) needs except the engine patch:
  - a spec md (layout, net file format, how UseFullNnue=0 would keep the residual net the default, incremental-update plan);
  - a trainer (new file, built on the v3b loader conventions and the FPOS format in files/06_jobD/format/);
  - a converter to the planned engine format, plus a pure-Python (or standalone C++ outside the engine tree) reference evaluator for that format;
  - a tiny smoke net trained on files/06_jobD/data32_sample/data32_sample_50k/ (synthetic, a pipeline check only).
  The engine integration is a later job after CR reviews A2 and this spec; it cannot be trained, reviewed and gated this week, and a large OFF-default drop is where default-build leaks hide.
- Inputs: L, B, files/07_nnue_context/, files/06_jobD/ (format, samples, trainer), files/03_nets/, your A2 doc.
- Deliver: forge_astra_A3_fullnnue_spec_<date>.md, forge_astra_A3_trainer_<date>.py, forge_astra_A3_converter_<date>.py, the reference evaluator, the smoke net + its sha256, report.
- Pass:
  - trainer → converter → reference evaluator agree within a stated float tolerance on 1k positions;
  - in the reference evaluator, incremental == full refresh on 200k positions with 0 mismatches;
  - reruns with a fixed seed reproduce the smoke net's sha256;
  - no engine patch and no file inside the lock tree;
  - any net trained from this is offline only and is never queued on our GPU without a CR queue diff and a crew vote. NO strength claim.
